## African Drumming  & Dancing Incursions, Workshops & Classes

# RHYTHM CULTURE – AFRICAN DRUM & DANCE

Sunshine Coast - Brisbane - Melbourne - Sydney - Perth - Adelaide

{% columns %}
{% column %}
Rhythm Culture brings the energy, excitement and connection of West African drumming and dance to people across Australia. We deliver interactive African drumming workshops, dance incursions, performances and classes for schools, businesses, community groups and people of all ages.

Whether you're planning a school incursion, a corporate team-building event, a kindergarten program or simply looking to learn something new, we have an experience for you!

[**Our Drum Sing Dance program**](/school-kindergarten/) brings together African drumming, singing and dancing in one action-packed experience. Students get hands-on with real African drums, learn traditional rhythms, explore movement and work together to create their own musical ensemble. It's a fantastic way to combine cultural learning, creativity, music and movement.

We also offer specialised African drumming and dance workshops for primary and secondary schools, kindergartens, early learning centres and vacation care programs.
{% /column %}
{% column %}
For businesses and organisations, our corporate drumming workshops provide a fun and energising way to build connections, encourage teamwork and bring people together.

Beyond our incursions, we run regular weekly African drumming and dance classes on the Sunshine Coast. We also host workshops, performances, community events and our annual Camp Afro Foli, bringing local and international artists together to share their knowledge and passion for West African music and dance.

At Rhythm Culture, we are passionate about sharing the rich traditions of West African music while creating opportunities for people to connect through rhythm and movement. Our professional artists bring experience, enthusiasm and a genuine love of what they do.

**From school incursions to corporate events, weekly classes and community workshops, we bring people together through the power of rhythm.**

Come and find your rhythm with Rhythm Culture!
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

{% columns align="center" %}
{% column %}
![A young girl playing an African drum](/media/2019/02/Wildlings-1389-e1550208803338.jpg)
{% /column %}
{% column %}
### Kindergarten & Early Childhood Incursions

Bring the excitement of African drumming, singing and dancing to your school or early learning centre! Rhythm Culture's **Drum Sing Dance program** offers an exciting, hands-on cultural experience that gets everyone involved. Through rhythm, music, movement and participation, students explore the vibrant traditions of West African music while developing valuable creative, physical and social skills.

For younger children, we make learning about rhythm playful, active and full of discovery! Through simple drumming patterns, songs, movement and interactive games, children explore sound, beat and rhythm. They develop listening skills, coordination, body awareness and self-expression. Most importantly, they have fun learning and participating together.
{% /column %}
{% column %}
![A child in a tiger costume playing a djembe](/media/2019/02/Wildlings-1921.jpg)
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

{% callout %}
Give your children the opportunity to belong, be involved, express themselves and discover the joy of rhythm with Rhythm Culture!
{% /callout %}

## Supporting the EYLF Through Music, Movement & Play

{% columns %}
{% column %}
### Supporting the Early Years Learning Framework (EYLF)

Rhythm Culture's African Drum Sing Dance incursions offer a rich, engaging learning experience that aligns with the Early Years Learning Framework (EYLF) – Belonging, Being and Becoming. Through music, movement, singing and shared participation, children explore, discover and learn in a fun and supportive environment.

Our interactive workshops create opportunities for children to develop a strong sense of identity and belonging as they participate, express themselves and experience the joy of creating music together. As children share rhythms, take turns, listen and respond to one another, they build relationships, develop social skills and strengthen their connection with others.
{% /column %}
{% column %}
Drumming, singing and dancing also support children's physical wellbeing, coordination, body awareness and confidence. Through playful exploration of sounds, beats and movement, children become curious and involved learners. They experiment, make discoveries, express ideas and develop their communication skills through music and movement.

Importantly, our program introduces children to the richness of West African music and dance traditions. This creates opportunities to explore cultural diversity, develop respect for different traditions and broaden their understanding of the world around them.

Our Drum Sing Dance incursions bring together creativity, cultural exploration, physical activity and social connection. They provide a meaningful opportunity for educators to extend children's learning through an experience that is joyful, inclusive and engaging.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

## An Experience Everyone Can Enjoy!

{% callout %}
At Rhythm Culture, we believe music and movement are for everyone. Our professional facilitators bring the drums, energy and enthusiasm to create an engaging experience for your group.
{% /callout %}

## AFRICAN DRUMMING INCURSIONS IS WHAT WE DO!

{% columns align="center" %}
{% column %}
Our African drumming and dance incursions are suitable for primary schools, high schools, kindergartens, early learning centres and vacation care programs. We adapt each experience to suit the age, abilities and interests of the group. From little ones discovering rhythm for the first time to high school students exploring complex rhythms and ensemble playing, everyone has an opportunity to participate.

### Primary & High School African Drumming Incursions

Students get hands-on with traditional African drums and percussion instruments. They learn rhythmic patterns, practise listening and develop their coordination. As the rhythms build, students work together to create an exciting musical ensemble. We also introduce traditional African songs, call-and-response and dance.

These workshops encourage teamwork, communication, concentration, creativity and confidence. Furthermore, students develop an appreciation of cultural diversity and explore the role of music and dance in different communities.
{% /column %}
{% column %}
![Primary school students drumming](/media/2017/12/CTA_box_HP-school.jpg)
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

{% columns align="center" %}
{% column %}
![Students singing and drumming at a school incursion](/media/2018/09/A08R7271-e1550205581543.jpg)
{% /column %}
{% column %}
### Curriculum Connections & Educational Benefits

Our African Drum Sing Dance incursions complement the Australian Curriculum, particularly The Arts learning areas of Music and Dance. Students explore rhythm, musical patterns, movement, creative expression, performance and cultural traditions.

The program also supports opportunities to develop personal and social capabilities, critical and creative thinking, and intercultural understanding.

For early childhood settings, our activities connect with the five learning outcomes of the Early Years Learning Framework (EYLF). These include identity, community, wellbeing, learning and communication.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

